==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|slēpan}}
* {{l|ang|slāpan}} {{qualifier|Anglian}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*slēpaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*slab-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*slap-||to be weak, limp, languid}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|slēpa|lang=ofs}} (West Frisian {{term|sliepe|lang=fy}}), Old Saxon {{term/t|osx|slāpan}} (Low German {{term|slapen|lang=nds}}), Dutch ''[[slapen]]'', Old High German ''[[slafan|slāfan]]'' (German ''[[schlafen]]''), Gothic {{term|𐍃𐌻𐌴𐍀𐌰𐌽|tr=slēpan|lang=got}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈslæːp.ɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=VII|head=slǣpan}} ({{Latinx|'''slǣpþ'''}} ‘he sleeps’; {{Latinx|'''slēp'''}} ‘he slept’; {{Latinx|'''slēpon'''}} ‘they slept’; {{Latinx|'''ġeslǣpen'''}} past participle)

# to [[sleep]]

